      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. Comments in line 611-613 explains that: we swap `scaled_ref_frame`, which obtains in line 577-580 using `av1_get_scaled_ref_frame` into `xd`.\n\n\"Scaled\" might be a bit confusing:\n- here in motion search, \"scaled ref frame\" (vs raw) means the reference frame that\u0027s scaled to the resolution of the current frame.\n- Outside here, \"scaled ref frame\" (vs unscaled) usually means the reference frame that\u0027s in a different resolution than the current frame.",
